    "result": "The bug was inverted logic in `Statement.get_type()` in `sqlparse/sql.py:433` — it used `!= T.Keyword.CTE` instead of `== T.Keyword.CTE`, so the WITH-clause branch that walks past CTE definitions to find the actual DML keyword never ran. Fixed by correcting the comparison; verified both `issue227` (CTE gettype) and `issue632` (comment between CTE clauses) scenarios now return `SELECT` as expected."
